(2275552, 309112, 18207, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the comments, it was nice to read them. Some answers from me to you:<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Are_62:</b></div><hr/><i>I would never think of leaving this much tree in a bitrd picture but this strikes me more as a tree picture with a bird in it</i></td></tr></table>That''s exactly why I decided to use this angle and not something else with a thin branch as in the original. Thanks.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by soup:</b></div><hr/><i> a chicadee/goldfinch cross? </i></td></tr></table>Very close, he''s a great tit, parus major.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by theSaj:</b></div><hr/><i>Would have liked it mroe if the left side was cropped out.</i></td></tr></table>Being this a tribute to the Bokeh winner, I must have kept something out of field of depth. This also helped me keeping the eyes on the tree and the birdie, not allowing them to wander around in a homogenously textured image.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sherpet:</b></div><hr/><i>This is just so good....I.love it....."WOW"..."WOW"..."WOW"...</i></td></tr></table>I know it''s not <i>that</i> good at all, but I like it better than most voters do. Thank you, anyway.</td>', 'Thank you for all the comments, it was nice to read them. Some answers from me to you: Originally posted by Are_62:I would never think of leaving this much tree in a bitrd picture but this strikes me more as a tree picture with a bird in itThat''s exactly why I decided to use this angle and not something else with a thin branch as in the original. Thanks. Originally posted by soup: a chicadee/goldfinch cross? Very close, he''s a great tit, parus major. Originally posted by theSaj:Would have liked it mroe if the left side was cropped out.Being this a tribute to the Bokeh winner, I must have kept something out of field of depth. This also helped me keeping the eyes on the tree and the birdie, not allowing them to wander around in a homogenously textured image. Originally posted by sherpet:This is just so good....I.love it....."WOW"..."WOW"..."WOW"...I know it''s not that good at all, but I like it better than most voters do. Thank you, anyway.', '2006-03-31 02:30:22.000000', NULL, 0),
