(2318173, 310497, 11942, '<td valign="top">Wow! I really like this pic! Great idea &amp; really creative! I totally  dissagree that it would be better if the background was more in focus - people are obsessed with things being in focus on this site - why can''t it be seen as art??<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mad_brewer:</b></div><hr/><i> Would have been better if the background was a bit more in focus. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Wow! I really like this pic! Great idea & really creative! I totally  dissagree that it would be better if the background was more in focus - people are obsessed with things being in focus on this site - why can''t it be seen as art?? Originally posted by mad_brewer: Would have been better if the background was a bit more in focus. ', '2006-04-17 08:13:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2320189, 310260, 14700, '<td valign="top">I was on vacation when this challenge happened... it just came to my attention that someone liked mine well enough to redo it for this challenge.<br/> <br/>I do have to say I think yours is much more artistic than mine. I really dig it.  I think that if you would have put this up in the origial challenge I was in you would have won it.  I think that voting might me harsher now than it was about two years ago.<br/> <br/>Well done, and thank you for the honor.<br/> <br/>btw - I used a lazer pointer to make the cat interested in the hole ;-) Cats are suckers!<br/> <br/>Joel</td>', 'I was on vacation when this challenge happened... it just came to my attention that someone liked mine well enough to redo it for this challenge. I do have to say I think yours is much more artistic than mine. I really dig it.  I think that if you would have put this up in the origial challenge I was in you would have won it.  I think that voting might me harsher now than it was about two years ago. Well done, and thank you for the honor. btw - I used a lazer pointer to make the cat interested in the hole ;-) Cats are suckers! Joel', '2006-04-17 20:24:06.000000', NULL, 0),
