(3023832, 309686, 57358, '<td valign="top">I think your photo turned out pretty good, awesome parody on the original  (also, in case no-one said anything, the best way I''ve found to do selective desat is the sponge tool - you can even set the percentage of desat to do with it and then you use it like a brush... I''m pretty sure you find it where your burn/dodge tool is...  or if you want black and white using gradient map, just make a layer with mask to single out the colored part... I always find that it''s easier for me to zoom in and use a brush type tool than to try to use a selection tool)<br/> <br/>anyway, glad you posted this in that forum... it''s the first time I''ve seen this photo and it made my morning  : )  you''re lucky to have such a fun husband!</td>', 'I think your photo turned out pretty good, awesome parody on the original  (also, in case no-one said anything, the best way I''ve found to do selective desat is the sponge tool - you can even set the percentage of desat to do with it and then you use it like a brush... I''m pretty sure you find it where your burn/dodge tool is...  or if you want black and white using gradient map, just make a layer with mask to single out the colored part... I always find that it''s easier for me to zoom in and use a brush type tool than to try to use a selection tool) anyway, glad you posted this in that forum... it''s the first time I''ve seen this photo and it made my morning  : )  you''re lucky to have such a fun husband!', '2006-11-12 13:13:19.000000', NULL, 0),
